      "message": "Why is this needed here? `test_add_object.cpp` never references `EM_CACHE_CONFIGURATION` directly.\n\nThe only consumer of this macro is `config_cache.cpp:12`, which is compiled into `entity_manager_lib` — not into this test binary. By the time test_add_object links against entity_manager_lib, config_cache.cpp has already been compiled with whatever value meson.build set:\n\n```\nallowed \u003d get_option(\u0027new-device-detection\u0027)\ncpp_args_em +\u003d \u0027-DEM_CACHE_CONFIGURATION\u003d\u0027 + allowed.to_string()\n```\n\nSo this `-DEM_CACHE_CONFIGURATION\u003dtrue` here is a no-op — it only affects the compilation of test_add_object.cpp, which doesn\u0027t use the macro. The test\u0027s actual behavior depends entirely on the `new-device-detection` option used when building entity_manager_lib (default true, but overridable). If that option is ever set to false, this test would fail despite this line claiming to force true.",
